  "result": [
    "The version-aware observer binds the full dictionary frame and EED item to the selected eight-byte handle interpretation and unchanged unique layer name. It retains the existing APPID, parent/ownership, entry, frame boundary and source-name checks.",
    "The staged output uses the shared layer-reference verifier for both standard objects and the MLINESTYLE owner, then requires output table identity and final reference closure. R13 uses explicit partial output; R14 uses strict output.",
    "Independent fresh ezdxf readback checked the ACAD group values HELLO, 42, layer 0 and three complete XYZ LINE endpoint pairs in all 24 ASCII/Binary outputs.",
    "Focused AddressSanitizer controls check missing, zero and wide targets; duplicate layer identity; source layer-name mutation; dictionary value mutation; exact layer-handle wire-bit mutation; destination preservation and corrected same-adapter retry. The generated AC1012/AC1014 regression harness passed in 42.11 seconds.",
    "Standard-object source capture and payload-correlation ASan selectors passed after correcting a pre-existing test expectation: resolving a layer clears the raw replay spelling, so the budget control now verifies both the unresolved and resolved states."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The byte order remains a caller-selected producer policy, not automatic identification. Strict whole-file AC1012 and native duplicate/merge semantics remain unqualified.",
    "These controls cover one layer and generated dictionary graphs; native AutoCAD, nondefault layer identities, other APPIDs, versions and graph profiles need their own evidence. No DWG/DXF files were committed."
  ]
